That’s completely normal 👍
Maven does NOT create settings.xml by default. You have to create it manually.

I’ll guide you step-by-step (bank/corporate-network friendly).


---

✅ Where settings.xml SHOULD Be

Windows (your case)

C:\Users\<your-username>\.m2\settings.xml

> If .m2 exists but settings.xml doesn’t → create it




---

✅ Step-by-Step: Create settings.xml

1️⃣ Go to .m2 directory

Press Win + R

Paste:

%USERPROFILE%\.m2

Press Enter


If .m2 folder does not exist, create it manually.


---

2️⃣ Create the file

Right-click → New → Text Document

Rename to:

settings.xml

⚠️ Make sure it is NOT settings.xml.txt



---

3️⃣ Open settings.xml and Paste This (Minimal Working)

<settings xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/SETTINGS/1.0.0"
          xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
          xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/SETTINGS/1.0.0
                              https://maven.apache.org/xsd/settings-1.0.0.xsd">

    <!-- Uncomment proxy section ONLY if your office network needs it -->
    <!--
    <proxies>
        <proxy>
            <id>corp-proxy</id>
            <active>true</active>
            <protocol>http</protocol>
            <host>YOUR_PROXY_HOST</host>
            <port>YOUR_PROXY_PORT</port>
            <nonProxyHosts>localhost|127.0.0.1</nonProxyHosts>
        </proxy>
    </proxies>
    -->

</settings>

✅ Save the file.


---

🔍 Verify Maven Picks It Up

Run in Command Prompt:

mvn help:effective-settings

If Maven prints settings → ✅ working.


---

🧪 Now Retry Your Build

mvn clean install -U


---

🚨 Important: If Build Still Fails

Check these in order:

✔ 1. Internet test

Open in browser:

https://repo.maven.apache.org/maven2

If this does NOT open, proxy is mandatory.


---

✔ 2. Corporate Proxy (Very Likely at SBI)

Ask IT team for:

Proxy host

Proxy port


Then uncomment proxy section and fill details.


---

✔ 3. Maven Version

mvn -version

Expected:

Maven 3.8+

Java 17+



---

🧠 Why This Happens in Corporate Projects

Banks & enterprises:

Block direct internet

Force internal proxy / Nexus / Artifactory


👉 Long-term solution:

Use internal Nexus repo

Configure mirror in settings.xml


Example (later stage):

<mirrors>
  <mirror>
    <id>nexus</id>
    <mirrorOf>*</mirrorOf>
    <url>http://internal-nexus/repository/maven-public/</url>
  </mirror>
</mirrors>


---

✅ Summary

✔ settings.xml missing → normal
✔ You created it correctly
✔ Retry build
✔ Add proxy only if needed


